# Cloudflare Pages redirects. Ignored by GitHub Pages, so this is safe to
# land before the migration and takes effect once Cloudflare serves the site.
#
# The app is a single-page app: it rewrites tab URLs client-side with
# history.pushState (/app/game-log, /app/stadiums, ...). Those paths have no
# real file. On GitHub Pages that meant a genuine HTTP 404 plus a JS bounce
# through 404.html. Cloudflare can serve the app shell directly with a 200,
# which is what the app already expects — tabFromLocation() parses the slug
# straight out of location.pathname, so deep links just work, with no
# redirect flash and no 404 status.
/app/*  /app/index.html  200

# Keep the dev docs off the public web. Cloudflare Pages serves every file in
# the repo, so without these CLAUDE.md (full build guide, architecture notes
# and roadmap) would be readable at momntsapp.com/CLAUDE.md even with the
# GitHub repo set to private. Repo visibility and site visibility are separate
# things. The GitHub Pages equivalent lives in _config.yml.
/CLAUDE.md   /404.html  404
/README.md   /404.html  404
/_config.yml /404.html  404
/.github/*   /404.html  404
